 6. Consequence: host() can never contain ':', '/', '?', '#', or a FIRST '@'. Membership of ':', '/', '?', '#' (and 0x00) in the charset is UNOBSERVABLE through this driver; treat them as rejected. '@' IS observably rejected. The '[::1]' anomaly is fully explained: 'http://[::1]:8080/x' -> host "[" (VALID), port_str ":1]:8080" -> stoi fails -> port invalid; 'http://[a:b]:80' -> host '[a' VALID, port invalid; 'http://[a]:80' -> host '[a]' VALID with port 80 valid.
